<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nana Olomu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanaya">Nana</a> Olomu was an Itsekiri merchant prince who served as governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> River in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a> from 1884 and controlled much of its palm-oil trade. His power over trade brought him into conflict with British officials, and in 1894 British forces destroyed his fortified town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebrohimi">Ebrohimi</a>. He was exiled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> and allowed to return in 1906.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nana-olomu.jpg" alt="Nana Olomu" width="320" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muyiwa OSIFUYE · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Chjef_Nana_of_Koko_and_Palace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
